The importance of an Employee Attrition Prediction project is that it solves a real business problem: employee turnover.

Why is it important?

Imagine a company has 1,000 employees. Every year, some employees leave. Replacing them can involve:

Recruiting a new person
Conducting interviews
Training the new employee
Losing productivity while the position is vacant
Losing experienced employees and their knowledge

An ML system can analyze employee data and identify patterns associated with employees who leave.

Example

Suppose the model finds that employees with:

Low job satisfaction
Frequent overtime
Low salary
Few promotion opportunities
Poor work-life balance

are more frequently associated with attrition in the historical dataset.

The company can then investigate those factors and take appropriate retention measures.



For your portfolio, you can describe the project as:

"A machine learning system that analyzes employee characteristics and workplace factors to predict attrition risk and identify patterns associated with employee turnover."


